#!/usr/bin/env node
// V2V fix 4 - agent-side translation safety. Apply on top of fix 2 and the fix 3 proxy files.
//   1. Nova Sonic events tracked by their documented fields (contentId, contentEnd.stopReason): every
//      sentence's audio waits for its own text to pass the checks; turn ends are detected again.
//   2. Microphone audio low-pass filtered before conversion to 16 kHz, for Nova Sonic and Transcribe
//      (sound above 8 kHz used to fold back into the speech band as distortion).
//   3. Restarts: wait for a fallback that is still playing; background noise to the customer switched
//      back on after a restart; drift counted once per sentence (restart after 3); restarts rate-limited.
//   4. Checks: assistant replies / talk about translating caught (ASSISTANT_REPLY) and more refusal
//      phrases; Spanish no longer accepted as the agent's English; echo repeats blocked; a sentence
//      that Transcribe splits into pieces is joined; the fallback never re-speaks an earlier sentence.
//   5. Translate + Polly fetched as soon as Transcribe has the sentence, so a fallback plays at once.
//   6. Logs: [SETTINGS] at start and on every change, [TIMING] fallback, [turn-end], [contentEnd],
//      and one [CALL-SUMMARY] line per call.
//   7. What Nova Sonic heard: when it hears the agent already in Spanish (every drift and every
//      assistant reply in the test calls started that way), that Spanish sentence is prepared at once
//      and spoken if Nova Sonic's output fails - no Translate, no wait for Transcribe. A Spanish output
//      that is not what it heard is replaced the same way ([MISMATCH]). Heard in English, the fallback
//      translates the agent's words as before. The customer's own voice picked up by the agent's
//      microphone is not played back to them. Logs: [HEARD], and the spoken text on [FALLBACK] lines.
//   8. Prompt rule 10: "if what you hear is already in <target language>, say it as it is".
//   9. Polly's Spanish voice is Lupe generative (falls back to neural if the region lacks it). The
//      proxy speaks text that is already in the target language without calling Translate.
//
// Run from the project root (the folder that contains cdk-stacks, webapp, proxy and SETUP.md):
//   node apply-v2v-fix-4.cjs            check only: reports what it would do, changes nothing
//   node apply-v2v-fix-4.cjs --apply    applies everything, or nothing if any check fails
//
// - Edits 7 existing webapp files and 1 proxy file (proxy/src/services/fallback.js) in place, and
//   creates 1 new file (webapp/utils/translationGuards.js). Each edit replaces one exact block of
//   text; if that block is not found exactly once, nothing is changed and the file is reported. Any
//   other changes you have in those files are kept.
// - Backs up every file it modifies or overwrites to v2v-backup-<timestamp>/ first.
// - Works with either Windows (CRLF) or Unix (LF) line endings, and is safe to run twice.
// - The deploy (cdk-stacks: npm run build:deploy:all) rebuilds the proxy image as well as the webapp.
